      "subject": "fix(knowledge): a Runtime restart no longer strips canonical promotion history (F-31)",
      "body": "On every Runtime start, rehydration rebuilt canonical items from their packages and overwrote the persisted record whenever the rebuilt copy differed. For Learning Records promoted automatically under ADR-0042 it always differed, because the promotion writes review evidence, review history, lifecycle history and supersession into the canonical record itself: six records lost that history at the 09:12 restart. Rehydration now restores only canonical items that are missing and never rewrites a persisted one; a Runtime start on the committed store leaves it byte-for-byte unchanged. The four committed records were restored from git; LR-2026-0005 and LR-2026-0006, damaged before they were ever committed, were rebuilt from their packages with the same fields GovernedCanonicalPromotionService writes, a method that reproduces the four committed records byte for byte.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AHtXdN7VRusNxTFHzk5uFe",
      "changedPaths": [
